UID:634938c4-eb81-47da-8636-f37b34f7db55
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=David 
 Caballero;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:david.caballero@code.berlin
URL:https://wiki.code.berlin/display/ID/LU
CREATED:20180919T130000Z
DESCRIPTION:\nAll times this LU is taking place\nWed 19.09. 15-19h\n\nLectu
 rer\nGerald Geilert \n\nBlurb\nIn this learning unit the hacking scene will
  be explored. The unit covers the wide spectrum from white hat to black hat
  hackers. We start off with Steven Levy’s hacker ethic\, which was embraced
  by the members of the Chaos Computer Club. Subsequently hacks by Boris Flo
 ricic (Tron)\, Karl Koch (Hagbard Celine) or Barnaby Jack will be discussed
 . Furthermore security issues will be addressed. In conclusion current prac
 tices of hacking will be debated.\n\nStudent Host\nEdit this doc to enter y
 our name. \nFirst come\, first serve.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20230106T222043Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:LU_60 What makes me a Hacker?
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-APPLE-TRAVEL-ADVISORY-BEHAVIOR:AUTOMATIC
