BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20210903T153000Z
DTEND:20210903T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20251202T224908Z
ORGANIZER;CN=Hanno Grimm:mailto:hanno.grimm@code.berlin
UID:7htnpaij79rt7d76i511agfb0h@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=da
 vid.caballero@code.berlin;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:david.caballero@code.berlin
CREATED:20210818T172141Z
DESCRIPTION:Dear students\,\n\nwe invite again to a Student General Assembl
 y. You might ask yourself why we choose to invite you at such unchristian h
 ours. Here's an explanation:\n\nWe have to vote on changes to the Rules of 
 Procedure regarding the eligibility of online voting. \n\nThe issue at hand
 : We can only vote on the eligibility of online votes in person (as online 
 votes are not eligible right now!)\n\nOur online votings over the last seme
 ster have been legitimized through the special laws put in place by the cit
 y of Berlin during the pandemic restrictions. \n\nTo be able to continue on
 line votings\, we have to pass an amendment to our Rules of Procedure to do
  so.\n\nAfter carefully picking a time where we can maximize the chance to 
 have enough students in physical presence to vote (we need at least 10% of 
 the entire student body present)\, we determined that this Semester Start G
 et Together is the time with most students on campus.\n\nSo: We will integr
 ate a mini-vote for 10mins during our Get Together. Bring your (student) fr
 iends! This is an important vote! Afterwards we celebrate together :)\n\nMo
 re information on the amendment will be shared over Slack in the coming day
 s.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230106T222550Z
LOCATION:CODE University of Applied Sciences\, Lohmühlenstraße 65\, 12435 B
 erlin\, Germany
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Student General Assembly
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
