ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=colin.
 boehning@code.berlin;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:colin.boehning@code.berlin
CREATED:20181117T200040Z
DESCRIPTION:https://codeuniversity.slack.com/archives/CCK2AD8L8/p1542485713
 009000\n\n*What will happen in the workshop?*\n\nEmpathy is the ability to 
 understand and feel another person’s perspectives\, experiences\, and point
 s of view. It is a very important skill for building truly inclusive web ap
 plications. But in designing and developing web applications our cognitive 
 biases often cloud our perspective.\n\nIn this workshop we will dive into t
 he story behind 3 personas with different disability spectrums\; permanent\
 , temporary and situational. Based on the examples the attendees will learn
  the basics about inclusiveness and will directly train their empathy skill
 s.\n\nThe attendees will be separated into groups and receive cards from th
 e game Questions and Empathy\, a strategic game to gain deeper insights int
 o these personas so we can develop accessible voice interfaces. Based on th
 e understanding we will gain\, the attendees will be able to develop a feat
 ure using the Speech Recognition API provided as part of the workshop.\n\n*
 What is the goal or outcome of the workshop?*\n\nLearn that empathy it’s no
 t only a skill but a powerful tool to better understand the users trying to
  interact with our web applications. Learn that understanding empathy as a 
 tool is a valuable asset\, but most importantly we will learn how to unders
 tand someone else feelings and perspectives.\n\nUsing the findings of the f
 irst half of the workshop\, we will start developing one feature using the 
 provided application that includes the Speech Recognition API as a starting
  point. We will understand that accessibility and inclusiveness are the cor
 e concerns of our web applications.\n\n*After the workshop\, how will I and
  my participants take the learning and activities forward?*\n\nBesides the 
 gained insights\, resources will be available to everyone in a Github repos
 itory for an unlimited time. This includes covered material\, the documente
 d results of the strategic game and the code of the developed feature.\n\nT
 he facilitator (that’s me grinning face) will provide a web application inc
 luding the Web Speech Recognition API for the second half of the workshop. 
 The participants are encouraged to fork and experiment with the application
  afterward and build their own features using the Web Speech Recognition AP
 I. The goal is for the participants to dive further into the topic of inclu
 sive and accessible web applications and contribute to the community with t
 heir own insights.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230106T222459Z
LOCATION:(Seminar Room)-CODE Campus-4-Scissors (25)
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Building Web Empathy - SinnerSchrader Workshop by Mauricio Palma
TRANSP:OPAQUE
