ORGANIZER;CN=calendar-invite@lu.ma:mailto:calendar-invite@lu.ma
UID:evt-kKzZjix2g53Au1H@events.lu.ma
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=David 
 Caballero;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:david.caballero@code.berlin
CREATED:20211005T040755Z
DESCRIPTION:Get up-to-date information at: https://lu.ma/event/evt-kKzZjix2
 g53Au1H?pk=g-qDUjsplVvChL2Fs\n\nClick to join: https://lu.ma/join/g-qDUjspl
 VvChL2Fs\n\nEvent Information:\n\nAbout event 📣\nADPList Coffee Hours Port
 folio Edition is where design mentors answer questions in a much more detai
 led and personal format. We get deep! Hop on with the mentors and ask your 
 design-related questions.\nCatch us on YouTube Live 📺:  https://youtu.be/z
 OVrGbg__5g\nFollow us on  LinkedIn  & tweet us your questions  @ADPList\nPo
 rtfolio Edition 🏆\nIt is a round-robin style where mentors take turns revi
 ewing portfolios submitted by the audience for 10-15mins and concluded with
  a short Q&A. Are you ready for this design critique session where we can a
 ll learn from each other's work and reflect on our own? We are!\nAbout Our 
 Mentors 🎙️\n🇨🇦  Seul Lee  - Sr. UX Design Specialist at Weavik\nSeul Lee
  (She/her) is a senior UX design specialist at Weavik where she works on di
 verse client projects in variety industries. She works from inception to la
 unch\, managing and forming teams within the organization\, and optimizing 
 their operational processes.\nFun Fact: She has a cute 5 months old kitty c
 alled Louie   and 10 different plants to take care of  😂\n🇨🇦  Timothy Li
   - Product Designer at theScore\nTim is Product Designer at theScore in To
 ronto\, working on building an engaging sports fan experience through our m
 edia and sports gaming mobile apps. Before that\, he’s helped teams improve
  their user experiences at Wattpad\, Rover Parking\, MobyTrip\, and other e
 arly-stage startups in Toronto.\nFun Fact: He’s run 2 marathons!  🏃‍♂️\nAb
 out Our Host 🎉\n🇺🇸  Ying Yao   -   Senior UX Designer at Honeywell\nYing
  (she/her) is a UX and product designer at Honeywell. She kicked off her ca
 reer creating digital solutions for Fortune 500 clients before transitionin
 g to enterprise UX to tackle B2B product challenges. In addition to being a
 n ADPList mentor\, she's also the co-organizer of  Ladies that UX Atlanta \
 , a design community focused on career growth\, community learning\, and bu
 ilding relationships among diverse women and non-binary folx.\nFun Fact: In
  her previous life\, Ying broadcasted smooth jams through the airwaves of A
 tlanta as a radio DJ  🎧\nDisclaimer: By participating in this event\, you 
 consent to interviews\, photography\, audio recording\, video recording and
  its/their release to be used for purposes that ADPList team deems fit to u
 se. You release the ADPList staff and all persons involved from any liabili
 ty connected with the taking\, recording\, digitizing\, or publication of i
 nterviews\, photographs\, images\, audio and/or video recordings.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230106T222358Z
LOCATION:https://lu.ma/join/g-qDUjsplVvChL2Fs
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:ADPList Coffee Hours: Portfolio Edition #14
TRANSP:OPAQUE
