UID:3e58a3n690s9qu9c2jhekark7s@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=zz
 -event-group-link-4970136896;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:zz-event-group-link-4970
 136896@app.code.berlin
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=da
 vid.caballero@code.berlin;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:david.caballero@code.berlin
CREATED:20190328T143021Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>For PM and SE Students / Groups will get split after an init
 ial introduction</b><br><br><b>A) 13:00 - 13:30 pm // Introduction to Digit
 al Product Teams at XING</b><br>What does Xing do\, where does it come from
  and where is it headed? What roles do you have\, how are teams organized a
 nd how do they work together? What processes or methodologies do you use\, 
 can you give some concrete examples of teams?<br><br><b>B) 13:30 - 14:30 pm
  // Career Trajectories for Product Managers &amp\; Software Engineers</b><
 br>Splitting the group into respective departments\, this talk is a deep di
 ve into what a start into a PM/SE career looks like\, how people progress i
 n their careers and what skills you are looking for when hiring new talent.
  What is the process of hiring\, what competencies do recruiters look for a
 nd how can students prepare for that? Please leave 15 minutes of questions 
 for this part.<br><br>// Note: You do not have to stay for part C) only bec
 ause you took part on A) and B) //<br><br><b>C) 15:00 - 16:00 pm // CV Chec
 kin (or) Speed-Dating-Job-Interview</b><br>This could be an opportunity to 
 do a quick interview for the summer internship program or an opportunity fo
 r students to do a mock interview with you and/or receive your valuable fee
 dback about their CVs.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230106T222054Z
LOCATION:Paper & Scissors
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:XING All Things Career for SE & PM 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
