BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20230320T160000Z
DTEND:20230320T165000Z
DTSTAMP:20251202T224908Z
ORGANIZER;CN=noreply@rainfocus.net:mailto:noreply@rainfocus.net
UID:prd.1661903922988001XWe5.1673974780610001AhUC.1658846gtcspring2023.nvid
 ia@rainfocus.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=David 
 Caballero;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:david.caballero@code.berlin
CREATED:20230220T142352Z
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to port Python data science and data engineering proj
 ects to the open-source\, GPU-accelerated RAPIDS suite with minimal code ch
 anges. We'll cover practical advice on how to massively accelerate workload
 s currently written using Pandas/scikit-learn/NumPy and related libraries b
 y running them on the GPU with RAPIDS. We'll discuss data manipulation\, an
 alytics\, machine learning\, and user-defined functions. Finally\, we'll go
  over common "gotchas" and things to watch out for when porting code or mai
 ntaining codebases that need to run on both GPU and CPU. By the end of the 
 talk\, you will be ready to begin converting real-world pipelines to run on
  GPU.\n\nPrior RAPIDS experience is not necessary\, but knowledge of Python
  will be important. 
LAST-MODIFIED:20230220T142357Z
LOCATION:Please visit https://register.nvidia.com/flow/nvidia/gtcspring2023
 /attendeeportal/page/schedule to access your schedule. Sessions open 15 min
 utes prior to the scheduled start time.
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:NVIDIA GTC Session
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
