DTEND:20210504T203000Z
DTSTAMP:20251202T224908Z
UID:v09ck61u0nt1mj43vtef88vtjk@google.com
CREATED:20210430T174830Z
DESCRIPTION:Join from a PC\, Mac\, iPad\, iPhone or Android device:\n    Pl
 ease click this URL to join. https://us02web.zoom.us/w/89968941713?tk=qWzZu
 XiHqPyJ-2OSiZOcoKayUZ10XSvnQi2kqiGIkSY.AG.lxisSEJ5k6JGgEpuWmT2UeipIpo5zSaCA
 _YI1KvjkzCdb_JZDsbzBS6W0fSfKdg7TfpQXddCsZG-ubLcsb3pBOM6FD1ge4dD.hdnNwuHQb_p
 7BqIA-7UYoQ.ncyzoESOxjSgHODt&pwd=MXM5bmNXNFVMM3R2dWpCR0d2WGNLdz09&uuid=WN_P
 rXaiApwQAypb-ZZN3UOBQ\n    Passcode: 031080\nDescription: NFT Aesthetics co
 ntinues “Net Aesthetics\,” a series of panels that seeks to examine how the
  internet is reshaping contemporary art. Where prior panels (presented in 2
 006\, 2008\, and 2013) responded to developments such as blogs\, social med
 ia\, and postinternet art\, this panel convenes artists to consider the imp
 lications of NFT marketplaces and platforms for artistic practice.\n\nNFTs 
 are unique (that is to say\, non-fungible) “tokens” that are assigned to di
 gital artworks and registered\, bought\, and sold via cryptocurrency blockc
 hains. Communities of practitioners from disparate scenes—including illustr
 ation\, fan art\, and creative code—have been sharing their work on NFT pla
 tforms for several years\, developing their own shared values and aesthetic
  languages. Yet for many outside of these communities\, the ascendancy of N
 FTs appears quite sudden. Artists now face questions as to how\, or if\, to
  translate their practice to this emerging context\, with its complex affor
 dances and limitations.  \n\nThis event convenes artists practicing 3D mode
 ling\, text\, software\, and digital painting\, representing a range of exp
 erience levels with NFTs\, to discuss the implications that NFTs have for t
 heir practices. Panelists include artists Harm van den Dorpel\, Auriea Harv
 ey\, Katherine Frazer\, Sara Ludy\, and Ryan Kuo\, who will each share thei
 r own work\, their engagement with NFTs\, and their views on the larger imp
 lications that NFTs hold for our understanding of art and culture as a whol
 e \n\nThis event is presented in conjunction with “World on a Wire\,” the f
 irst exhibition in a new partnership between Hyundai Motor Company and Rhiz
 ome of the New Museum to showcase leading digital art globally. \n\nAccessi
 bility: we strive to make our programs as accessible as possible. For full 
 accessibility information\, including services available by request\, pleas
 e visit this page: newmuseum.org/pages/view/accessibility\n\nOr One tap mob
 ile:\n    +13017158592\,\,89968941713#\,\,\,\,*031080# US (Washington DC)\n
     +13126266799\,\,89968941713#\,\,\,\,*031080# US (Chicago)\n\nOr join by
  phone:\n    Dial(for higher quality\, dial a number based on your current 
 location):\n        US: +1 301 715 8592  or +1 312 626 6799  or +1 346 248 
 7799  or +1 669 900 6833  or +1 929 205 6099  or +1 253 215 8782 \n    Webi
 nar ID: 899 6894 1713\n    Passcode: 031080\n    International numbers avai
 lable: https://us02web.zoom.us/u/kd9WCITcEc\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20210504T185022Z
LOCATION:https://us02web.zoom.us/w/89968941713?tk=qWzZuXiHqPyJ-2OSiZOcoKayU
 Z10XSvnQi2kqiGIkSY.AG.KX-VLI-1cZYSCd6-9hJQAoDxh7AQblHCWUz11X2xATVHHz66CCDD5
 kwrN6rJhmzcppiAjIqhJBhzTdHpEofhUqpLW-g5QF95.Rm8HxQ8NTvDNsJokOcuPeg.V_72QZwl
 MdEYkWmj&pwd=MXM5bmNXNFVMM3R2dWpCR0d2WGNLdz09&uuid=WN_PrXaiApwQAypb-ZZN3UOB
 Q
SEQUENCE:0
