CREATED:20191030T112234Z
DESCRIPTION:Dear members of the Interaction Design study program\,<br><br>W
 e would like to invite you to the annual General Assembly for the ID depart
 ment. This is a great opportunity for you to play an active role in shaping
  your course of studies and a good chance for us to get your vote for your 
 study program. So please join us!&nbsp\;<br><br>Some background information
  for you\; according to CODE’s Basic Regulations §21\, once per year the Ge
 neral Assembly of each study program must meet.<br><br><b>Some of the tasks
  of the General Assembly include:</b><br>the election of the members of the
  Senate nominated by the study program\,<br>participation in the further de
 velopment of the study program.<br><br><b>Topics that we already have on th
 e agenda for discussion include:</b><br>- Proposal for a new Program Coordi
 nator<br>- Proposal for a new Academic Senate representative<br>- Open disc
 ussion (15 minutes)<br><br>If there is a topic related to your study progra
 m that you would like to discuss in this meeting\, please approach your stu
 dent representative or the Program Coordinator who will collect topics for 
 the open discussion until the 11th of November.&nbsp\;<br><br>An updated ag
 enda will be distributed via SLACK the day before the meeting is scheduled 
 to take place.<br><br>We hope to see you there and look forward to your inp
 ut.<br><br>Yours sincerely\,<br>&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\;<br>Harmut Wöh
 lbier&nbsp\;<br>ID Program Coordinator
LAST-MODIFIED:20240601T092644Z
LOCATION:--4-Jungle (40)
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:ID General assembly
TRANSP:OPAQUE
