DTEND:20251001T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20251202T224908Z
ORGANIZER;CN=Laurin Notemann:mailto:laurin.notemann@code.berlin
UID:57b41bm8ivckf9pi4732o77i5s@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=da
 vid.caballero@code.berlin;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:david.caballero@code.berlin
X-GOOGLE-CONFERENCE:https://meet.google.com/ecr-agnm-can
CREATED:20250925T163505Z
DESCRIPTION:Hey everyone\,<br><br>We need you at the next General Assembly 
 of all our students on October 1st\, next Wednesday (online attendance will
  be possible) at 18:00. You also received a calendar invite\, and it was an
  intentional decision to ping you twice. We know this is quite spontaneous\
 , but we really need as many students as possible to attend in order for th
 is to be a formal General Assembly.<br><br><a href="https://github.com/code
 university/student-council/pull/13" target="_blank">Here</a> you can check 
 out the official changes we are planning to make.<br><br>As time goes by\, 
 our responsibilities as students have adjusted and together with the Friend
 s of CODE e.V.\, we now have stronger Student Governance than ever before (
 things are still taking shape\, but keep an eye out for new updates in that
  regard over the next few weeks). To accommodate these changes\, bring some
  accountability back to the Student Council\, and make it a bit leaner\, we
  have worked on a change that reduces the seats from 14 to 7 with more spec
 ific\, dedicated roles:<br><br>1. President (spokesperson &amp\; lead)<br>2
 . Alumni Relations<br>3. Admissions &amp\; Study Experience<br>4. Community
  Builder<br>5. Marketing<br>6. Entrepreneurship<br>7. Partnerships<br><br>A
 dditionally\, four of these elected Student Council representatives will al
 so have a seat in the academic senate.<br><br>As I will share information o
 n the responsibilities of the Friends of CODE e.V.\, you might see some ove
 rlapping tasks/departments\, which will then be handled internally (either 
 someone from the Friends of CODE e.V. representatives will also be in the S
 tudent Council\, or the SC representative will be included in the Friends o
 f CODE e.V.). The point here is that we are not interested in having two se
 parate entities that work independently\, but rather a strong\, united Stud
 ent Governance.<br><br>These changes to the Student Council's statutes can 
 only be made by a General Assembly\, hence our invitation for next Wednesda
 y. At the same time\, this event will also function as a Town Hall Meeting\
 , so if you have any questions\, bring them\, and we will try to answer the
 m.<br><br>It should also be noted that the new election will take place som
 etime in October\, which we will\, of course\, announce again as we get aro
 und to actually having them.<br><br>PS: This is a first reminder that we wi
 ll have another amazing Halloween Party this year on October 31st. We will 
 share more information shortly.<br>PPS: Give Max a follow on GitHub<br><br>
 Your Student Council\n\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~
 :~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~::-\nJoin with Google Meet: https://meet.g
 oogle.com/ecr-agnm-can\nOr dial: (DE) +49 30 300195255 PIN: 280011648#\nMor
 e phone numbers: https://tel.meet/ecr-agnm-can?pin=5472445587142&hs=7\n\nLe
 arn more about Meet at: https://support.google.com/a/users/answer/9282720\n
 \nPlease do not edit this section.\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~
 :~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~::-
LAST-MODIFIED:20250925T163758Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:General Assembly/Town Hall Meeting 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
